  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical charged spheres are suspended by strings of equal lengths. The string make an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with each other. When suspended in a liquid of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the angle remains same. If density of material of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the dielectric constant of the liquid is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7b33333b-f203-4cf1-b181-c629a462bfdc.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 128px;\"/></p><p>For first case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math> and </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>For second case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math> </p><p>From Eq. (i) &amp; (ii), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>k</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi>k</mi><mo> </mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>k</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
